{"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 9, 22]], "date-time": "2026-09-22T18:15:54Z", "timestamp": 1790100954287, "version": "4.0.1"}, "reference-count": 60, "publisher": "Wiley", "issue": "1", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2019, 3, 1]], "date-time": "2019-03-01T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1551398400000}, "content-version": "vor", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/"}], "funder": [{"name": "GABI-Wheat and VALID", "award": ["0315067"], "award-info": [{"award-number": ["0315067"]}]}, {"name": "GABI-Wheat and VALID", "award": ["0315947"], "award-info": [{"award-number": ["0315947"]}]}, {"name": "German Federal Ministry of Education and Research"}], "content-domain": {"domain": ["acsess.onlinelibrary.wiley.com"], "crossmark-restriction": true}, "short-container-title": ["The Plant Genome"], "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2019, 3]]}, "abstract": "<jats:sec>\n                    <jats:label/>\n                    <jats:p>\n                      <jats:italic>Septoria tritici</jats:italic>\n                      blotch (STB) caused by the fungus\n                      <jats:italic>Zymoseptoria tritici</jats:italic>\n                      is a devastating foliar disease of wheat (\n                      <jats:italic>Triticum aestivum</jats:italic>\n                      L.) that can lead to substantial yield losses. Quantitative genetic resistance has been proposed as a durable strategy for STB control. In this study, we dissected the genetic basis of STB infection in 371 European wheat varieties based on 35k and 90k single nucleotide polymorphism marker arrays. The phenotypic data analyses suggested that large genetic variance exists for STB infection with a broad\u2010sense heritability of 0.78. Genome\u2010wide association studies (GWAS) propose the highly quantitative nature of STB infection with potential associations on chromosomes 1A, 1B, 2D, 4A, 5A, 6A, 6D, 7A, and 7B. Increased marker density in GWAS by combining markers from both arrays helped to detect additional markers explaining increased genotypic variance. Linkage disequilibrium analyses revealed genes with a possible role in disease resistance. The potential of genomic prediction (GP) assessed via two models accounting for additive effects and additive plus epistatic interactions among the loci suggested the possibility of genomic selection for improved STB resistance. Genomic prediction results also indicated that the higher\u2010order epistatic interactions are not abundant and that both marker platforms are equally suitable for GP of STB infection. Our results provide further understanding of the quantitative genetic nature of STB infection, serve as a resource for marker\u2010assisted breeding, and highlight the potential of genomic selection for improved STB resistance.\n                    </jats:p>\n                  </jats:sec>", "DOI": "10.3835/plantgenome2018.05.0029", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2018, 11, 29]], "date-time": "2018-11-29T17:57:45Z", "timestamp": 1543514265000}, "update-policy": "https://doi.org/10.1002/crossmark_policy", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 55, "title": ["Genome\u2010wide Association Mapping and Prediction of Adult Stage\n                    <i>Septoria tritici</i>\n                    Blotch Infection in European Winter Wheat via High\u2010Density Marker Arrays"], "prefix": "10.1002", "volume": "12", "author": [{"given": "Quddoos H.", "family": "Muqaddasi", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "Leibniz Institute of Plant Genetics and Crop Plant Research (IPK) 06466 Stadt Seeland OT Gatersleben Germany"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Yusheng", "family": "Zhao", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Leibniz Institute of Plant Genetics and Crop Plant Research (IPK) 06466 Stadt Seeland OT Gatersleben Germany"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Bernd", "family": "Rodemann", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Julius K\u00fchn Institute (JKI) 38104 Braunschweig Germany"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "J\u00f6rg", "family": "Plieske", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "TraitGenetics GmbH 06466 Stadt Seeland OT Gatersleben Germany"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Martin W.", "family": "Ganal", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "TraitGenetics GmbH 06466 Stadt Seeland OT Gatersleben Germany"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Marion S.", "family": "R\u00f6der", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Leibniz Institute of Plant Genetics and Crop Plant Research (IPK) 06466 Stadt Seeland OT Gatersleben Germany"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "311", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2019, 3]]}, "reference": [{"key": "e_1_2_8_2_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1094/PHYTO.2003.93.9.1158"}, {"key": "e_1_2_8_3_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1094/PHYTO.2004.94.11.1198"}, {"key": "e_1_2_8_4_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.2135/cropsci2004.1403"}, {"key": "e_1_2_8_5_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/s00122-004-1709-6"}, {"key": "e_1_2_8_6_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1111/pbi.12635"}, {"key": "e_1_2_8_7_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1016/S0022\u20102836(05)80360\u20102"}, {"key": "e_1_2_8_8_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1111/j.1365\u20103059.2009.02118.x"}, {"key": "e_1_2_8_9_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/s001220100668"}, {"key": "e_1_2_8_10_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.18637/jss.v067.i01"}, {"key": "e_1_2_8_11_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/s00122\u2010007\u20100603\u20104"}, {"key": "e_1_2_8_12_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI":